Find Sum of Range  [l……….r] where(l<=r) using Prefix sum. 

Explanation:
In this problem, we need to find the sum of all elements between indices l and r (inclusive).
Instead of calculating the sum every time by looping from l to r, we first create a Prefix Sum array.
prefix[i] stores the sum of all elements from index 0 to i. 
Formula: prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] + arr[i]

Once the prefix array is built:
    If l == 0, the required sum is simply prefix[r].
    Otherwise, subtract the sum before index l from the sum till r:
    Sum(l...r) = prefix[r] - prefix[l-1]

This works because:
    prefix[r] contains the sum from 0 to r.
    prefix[l-1] contains the sum from 0 to l-1.
    Subtracting them leaves only the sum from l to r.

Code:
class Solution {

    static int rangeSum(int[] arr, int l, int r) {

        int[] prefix = new int[arr.length];

        prefix[0] = arr[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
            prefix[i] = prefix[i - 1] + arr[i];
        }

        if (l == 0)
            return prefix[r];

        return prefix[r] - prefix[l - 1];
    }
}
